# Project format

This repo is a public catalog of browser games. Each project is a single-page HTML app opened in the browser.

## Layout

```text
public/
  index.html              # hub: table of contents / project list
  <project-slug>/
    index.html            # that project's landing page (the playable game)
```

- One folder per project. Slug is lowercase kebab-case (`space-runner`, not `Space Runner`).
- The project's landing page is `public/<project-slug>/index.html`.
- Do not put a project at the repo root or as a lone file next to `public/index.html`.
- Extra assets for a project (sounds, textures) stay inside that project's folder.

Public URLs (after merge to `main`):

- Hub: `https://yamper.anatoly-yevtushenko.workers.dev/`
- Project: `https://yamper.anatoly-yevtushenko.workers.dev/<project-slug>/`

## After every iteration

When finishing work on a prompt:

1. Create or update `public/<project-slug>/index.html` so the game is playable in a browser.
2. Update `public/index.html` so the hub table of contents lists every project and links to its landing page (`/<project-slug>/`). Add a row for a new project; keep title and short description in sync if they changed.
3. Then follow the trunk-based merge workflow.

## Technical guidelines

- Projects are mostly video games.
- Use **Three.js** for visualization, effects, and drawing. Load it from a CDN with an import map. Pin `three@0.185.1` (same version for `three` and `three/addons/`). Do not use a bundler or npm for game pages.
- Load JavaScript libraries from a CDN. Do not embed, vendor, or copy library source into the repo unless the user asks. Pin versions on the CDN (import maps or versioned script URLs).
- Each game page is self-contained HTML opened directly in the browser. Inline CSS and a `<script type="module">`. No build step.
- The hub `public/index.html` is a table of contents only. Do not turn it into a game.

Example import map:

```html
<script type="importmap">
{
  "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.185.1/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.185.1/examples/jsm/"
  }
}
</script>
```
